  "rendering": {
    "paintMetricsNote": "firstContentfulPaintMs and lcpMs are null at most widths because the browser never emitted those entries, not because they were not collected. The homepage animates its eyebrow, h1, lead, buttons and note in from opacity: 0 in CSS (site.css lines 566-569 and 150), and Chromium excludes anything painted while fully transparent from both First Contentful Paint and Largest Contentful Paint candidacy. The result is a page with a first paint and no contentful paint: Lighthouse's own trace engine throws LanternError: NO_LCP, and its largest-contentful-paint-element audit identifies no element, while still reporting an LCP time. Real-user monitoring (CrUX, or any RUM using the web vitals API) would report no LCP for this page at all. This is the condition on the live site today and the motion layer inherits it; it is not caused by the motion layer, and equally, replacing the hero is the opportunity to fix it.",
